Sludge Treatment and Disposal — Andreoli, von Sperling and Fernandes (@wu-bw6: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_01W2VM1NE64Y1FDRJRM0RYKYY4
Cleverson Vitorio Andreoli, Marcos von Sperling and Fernando Fernandes. Biological Wastewater Treatment Series, volume 6, IWA Publishing, 2007. [Persistent publisher reference](https://doi.org/10.2166/9781780402130).

Read the entire solids-management account. Track dry solids and water through thickening, stabilization, dewatering, transport and the receiving route. Connect the treatment choice with pathogen reduction, contaminants, storage, weather and the evidence required for the intended destination.

The publisher lists the series as open-access. Preserve this work's actual rights and component notices. Historical disposal practices or criteria must be compared with current jurisdictional requirements; a sludge mass balance does not establish suitability for land application.

